  "text": "CDC Public Health Guide: Sleep Hygiene and Health | Publisher: Centers for Disease Control\nBasics of Good Sleep Hygiene\nGood sleep hygiene refers to habits that support consistent,\nuninterrupted, quality sleep.\nRecommended Sleep Hygiene Habits: - Be Consistent: Go to bed at the same\ntime each night and get up at the same time each morning, including on\nweekends. - Environment: Make sure your bedroom is quiet, dark, relaxing,\nand at a comfortable temperature. - Electronic Devices: Remove TVs,\ncomputers, and smartphones from the bedroom; avoid screen exposure 30-60\nminutes before bed. - Avoid Large Meals & Stimulants: Avoid heavy meals,\ncaffeine, and alcohol before bedtime.\nPage 1 of 4 | Official Educational Resource",
